# README Requirements

Keep `README.md` user-focused. Align with `project-overview.mdc` and `implementation.mdc`.

## Required sections (order)

1. **Title & description** — GNU `head`-compatible (GNU coreutils `head` 9.4);
   prints the first 10 lines (or `-n NUM` lines / `-c NUM` bytes, or all but
   the last NUM with `-NUM`) of each FILE to stdout; reads stdin when no FILE
   or `-`; raw `read(2)` / `write(2)` copy loop, heap used only to hold back
   the tail of a pipe for negative counts.
   - **Versions** note: v1.0.0 (tag) = POSIX-style subset; v2.0.0 = GNU-compatible.

2. **Build**
   - `make`, `make debug`, `make test`, `make clean`, optional `make install`
   - Artefacts: **`build/head-toto`**, **`build/head-toto-debug`**,
     **`build/tests/test_core`**; mention `build/.gitkeep` / `build/tests/.gitkeep`
   - **Linux / WSL:** `make clean && make && make test` then `./build/head-toto FILE`
   - **Windows:** Git Bash or MSYS2 **UCRT64**; `pacman -S make mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc`
   - Explain Makefile **`_O_BINARY` probe**: POSIX vs Windows binary-mode I/O; UCRT64 `gcc` on `PATH`
   - Native Windows `.exe` under `build/` runs in UCRT64, Git Bash, cmd, PowerShell

3. **Usage**
   - Show invocations as `./build/head-toto` (or installed `head-toto`)
   - Synopsis: `head-toto [OPTION]... [FILE]...`
   - Options table: `-n` / `--lines=[-]NUM`, `-c` / `--bytes=[-]NUM`,
     `-q` / `--quiet` / `--silent`, `-v` / `--verbose`, `-z` / `--zero-terminated`,
     `--help`, `--version`
   - NUM syntax: optional `+`, digits, multiplier suffix table; leading `-` =
     all but the last NUM; obsolete `-NUM` form (first argument only)
   - Default is 10 lines; last `-n` / `-c` wins; `-` means stdin
   - Headers `==> NAME <==` shown for multiple FILEs unless `-q`; forced with `-v`
   - `-v` is verbose (not version); long options may be abbreviated (`--v` is
     ambiguous); options are processed in order (first `--help` / `--version` wins)
   - Examples: single file, multiple files, `-c`, `-n -K`, a suffix, `-NUM`,
     pipe from stdin
   - **Differences from GNU `head`:** only the remaining deliberate ones listed in
     `project-overview.mdc` (program name / `--version` / `--help` text, write
     error wording, platform `<reason>` texts, no `---presume-input-pipe`)

4. **Exit codes**
   - `0`: success — every FILE copied (or `--help` / `--version`)
   - `1`: error — usage error, any FILE failed to open/read, or write failure
   - Unreadable FILEs are reported on stderr and the remaining FILEs are still processed
   - stderr: `head-toto: cannot open '<file>' for reading: <reason>`,
     `head-toto: error reading '<file>': <reason>`,
     `head-toto: error writing 'standard output': <reason>`

5. **Layout** — brief tree matching actual repo (include `LICENSE.txt`,
   `c_version.txt`, `build/.gitkeep`, `build/tests/.gitkeep`):
   - `include/head_toto.h` + `head_toto_{emit,cli,count,io}.h`
   - `src/main.c` + `head_toto_{emit,cli,count,io,run}.c`
   - `tests/test_runner.c` + `test_{count,copy,elide}_*.c` → `build/tests/test_core`
   - Note that unit tests run on both Linux and Windows builds (no `SKIP:`)

## Do not document in README

- Internal chain-of-thought comment blocks
- `-Werror` flag rationale (lives in `Makefile` comments)
- Author/licence banners on `--version` (binary prints `head-toto <version>` only)
- `parse_long()`, `try_write_all()`, `try_read()`, or other static helper
  names unless briefly needed for contributors

## Style

- Fenced `sh` blocks for commands.
- No emojis unless the user asks.
- Keep prose minimal.
